<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Novocherkassk treasure</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century CE</span> · Also known as Khokhlach treasure</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/novocherkassk">Novocherkassk</a> treasure is a hoard of Sarmatian gold found in 1864 in the Khokhlach kurgan at Novocherkassk on the lower Don in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. Dating from the first century CE and probably from the burial of a noblewoman, it includes a gold diadem set with amethysts, garnets and a Greek cameo, and vessels and ornaments in a polychrome animal style. It is held in the Hermitage Museum.</p></div>
